      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never loading it into the Hub process itself**. Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (Ingest agent or Query agent) immediately before they start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n\nThis design means that even if the Hub process is compromised or misbehaves, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only transiently in the short-lived child process that actually needs it to call the Anthropic API.",
